{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 29, :comments ["<b>A dwelling house in a walled city.</b> A house inside a city surrounded by a wall from the days of Joshua son of Nun (Sifra)." "<b>And its redemption shall be.</b> Since it is stated regarding a field that he may redeem it from two years onward whenever he wishes, and during the first two years he cannot redeem it, it was necessary to specify here that it is the reverse — that if he wished to redeem in the first year he may redeem it, and after this he may not redeem it." "<b>And its redemption shall be.</b> That of a house." "<b>Days.</b> The days of a full year are called 'days,' and likewise ״תֵּשֵׁב הַנַּעֲרָה אִתָּנוּ יָמִים״ (Genesis 24)."], :book :leviticus, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 25, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T09:08:21.959161801Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}